1. Introduction to MySQL
MySQL is a widely-used Relational Database Management System (RDBMS) that utilizes Structured Query Language (SQL) to interact with databases. It is known for its ACID compliance, which ensures reliable transaction processing.

Atomicity: Ensures that a transaction is all-or-nothing. If any part of the transaction fails, the entire transaction is rolled back.

Durability: Guarantees that once a transaction is committed, it remains so even in the event of a system crash.

